# px4-sim-stack configuration.
# Copy this file to .env and edit it. `make preflight` fills in the host values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- host identity
# The sim container writes build output into the bind-mounted PX4 tree. These
# values must match your host user, or the output belongs to root.
HOST_UID=1000
HOST_GID=1000

# The host group that owns /dev/input/event*. The qgc container joins it so
# QGroundControl can read a joystick. `make preflight` reads the real value
# from `getent group input`.
INPUT_GID=107

# The host group that owns /dev/dri/renderD128 on a Jetson. The aircraft
# container joins it, beside video and dialout, so a uid 1000 process can
# open the GPU nodes. `./px4sim doctor` reads the real value from
# `getent group render`.
RENDER_GID=104

# X11 forwarding. `make x11` writes the cookie file.
# Keep this inside the project. Docker turns a missing bind-mount source into
# a directory, and one under /tmp ends up owned by root and needs sudo.
#
# This file does not set DISPLAY. Both front doors export it over their own
# environment. A value here would pin every container to one display, and hide
# the display of the session that starts them. compose.yaml defaults it to :0.
XAUTH_FILE=./.xauth

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ flight code
# Where 5g_drone, cdcl_umd_msgs and MAVInsight are checked out. The onboard and
# offboard images build that workspace with colcon, so the sources stay in
# their own git remote and nothing is mounted at run time. A change there needs
# `./px4sim build onboard offboard`.
ROS2_WS_DIR=../ros2_ws

# GPS-free bench reference. Leave disabled for every normal run. Enable only
# through `./px4sim ui` after stopping the stack and typing the confirmation
# phrase; it publishes configured home telemetry but never changes PX4 state.
BENCH_MODE=false
BENCH_HOME_LAT=38.313294
BENCH_HOME_LON=-76.55221
BENCH_HOME_ALT=8.1432
BENCH_FIDUCIAL_LAT=38.3133004
BENCH_FIDUCIAL_LON=-76.5522071
BENCH_FIDUCIAL_ALT=8.1232

# Where chimera-deploy is checked out. ros-base builds the MAVROS patch from
# remote/mavros_patch there, against its mavros and angles submodules. Run
# `git submodule update --init submodules/mavros submodules/angles` there first.
# Every ros-base build needs this path, MAVROS_PATCH=0 included, because docker
# resolves a named build context before it reads the Dockerfile. The submodules
# are needed only when MAVROS_PATCH=1.
CHIMERA_DEPLOY_DIR=../chimera-deploy
# 0 leaves MAVROS as apt ships it. PX4 v1.18 then answers no capabilities and
# the waypoint plugin sends MISSION_ITEM floats. See docs/uas-contract.md.
MAVROS_PATCH=1

# The detector and classifier artifacts. 5g_drone owns them:
# perception_models/ there holds one directory per machine that builds engines,
# and scripts/fetch_models.py in that repo fills the one belonging to this
# machine. Mount the WHOLE tree -- the group directories link into shared/ with
# relative symlinks, which dangle if only one of them is mounted.
ONBOARD_MODEL_DIR=${ROS2_WS_DIR}/src/5g_drone/perception_models
# One more parameter file, loaded after every other, naming what only this
# machine has. `local` is the symlink fetch_models.py points at this machine's
# group, so this line is the same on the Orin and on either laptop. A machine
# with nothing of its own to say has no such file and the entry point says so
# and carries on. See modules/onboard/models/README.md.
ONBOARD_PARAMS_FILE=/models/local/params.yaml
# The airframe on a real aircraft. deploy_onboard.sh writes this from UAS_NUM.
# v3 carries the SCF4 zoom lens; v2 has the fixed, two-axis gimbal.
# UAS_MODEL=v3

# ------------------------------------------------------------ component versions
# Change one line to test a different upstream version. See docs/development.md.
PX4_REF=v1.17.0
QGC_REF=v5.0.8
GZ_DISTRO=harmonic
MEDIAMTX_TAG=1
XRCE_AGENT_REF=v2.4.2

# Which DeepStream release the companion and the ground station are built from.
#
# Leave it empty. The answer is DeepStream 7.1 on Ubuntu 22.04 with ROS 2
# Humble, because that is what the aircraft is -- a Jetson Orin on 22.04 -- and
# because cdcl_umd_msgs does not decode across a distribution change. Jazzy
# adds a field to sensor_msgs/Range, which sits inside TargetBoxArray ahead of
# the box array, so a Humble vehicle and a Jazzy ground station exchange frames
# that arrive with an empty box list and no error at all.
#
# What DOES vary with the machine is TensorRT, and nothing here has to say so.
# DeepStream 7.1 ships TensorRT 10.3, which emits kernels up to Hopper. On a
# newer card it parses the model, reports `Unsupported SM`, builds no engine
# and dies -- while the streams keep decoding, so the only thing anyone sees is
# a detector that never fires. scripts/ds-select.sh reads the compute
# capability and puts a newer TensorRT in the same 22.04 image where one is
# needed. An Orin at 8.7 never triggers it and builds exactly what it always
# built. `./px4sim doctor` prints what this machine chose.
#
# Setting this to 8.0 or 9.0 is possible and builds ROS 2 Jazzy, which breaks
# the fleet as described above. ds-select.sh says so when you do.
DS_VERSION=
# An image outright, when it is a rebuild or a mirror rather than an NVIDIA tag.
# The release is read back out of its tag.
# DS_IMAGE=

# ------------------------------------------------------------ which machine
# One file serves three machines. UAS_BASE says which world the numbers
# belong to, and COMPOSE_PROFILES says what runs. Set the pair for this
# machine and leave the other pairs commented. ./px4sim refuses a file where
# the two disagree.
#
# The simulator, on one laptop. Vehicles are uas11 upwards, the ground
# station is domain 70 and everything lives on simnet. ./px4sim adds `sim`,
# a router and a companion profile for each vehicle in UAS_FLEET. The other
# profiles are `xrce`, `qgc-dev` and `scenegen`, and `./px4sim genscene`
# selects scenegen itself.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=sim,offboard
UAS_BASE=10
#
# The real ground station. The offboard image runs as `ground` on the host
# network, beside the native mavlink-router (127.0.0.1:14402) and lcam
# (8554). UAS_FLEET names the complete model mapping. Set UAS_ACTIVE to the
# UAS numbers actually airborne so the ground does not start MAVROS, DS, and
# visualization nodes for absent aircraft (for example: UAS_ACTIVE="3").
# The scene this station draws stands in "the scene" below, not here: this
# file is read from the top down, so a second SCENE line there would win over
# one here and the site would change without a word.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=ground
# UAS_BASE=0
# UAS_FLEET="chimera_v3"
# UAS_ACTIVE="1"
# GROUND_DOMAIN=60
# RTSP_BASE=rtsp://127.0.0.1:8554
#
# The aircraft. One onboard service on the host network, beside the native
# mavlink-router and rcam. UAS_NUM comes from /etc/environment, which
# chimera-deploy/deploy.sh writes, and is not repeated here. The whole fleet
# is listed so the number resolves to an airframe on any vehicle.
# The scene stands in "the scene" below, and is the one the ground station
# carries: both sides cast the camera ray at one ground.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=aircraft
# UAS_BASE=0
# UAS_FLEET="chimera_v3 chimera_v3 chimera_v2 chimera_v2"
# ONBOARD_LENS_DEVICE=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-Kurokesu_Kurokesu_SCF4-M_48F477A9394D-if00

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- the fleet
# One entry for each vehicle, in UAS number order: uas11 first. Each entry names
# a model in modules/sim/scenes/models/. The count decides how many PX4 SITL
# instances, mavlink-routers, companions and video streams the stack brings up.
#
# compose.yaml carries a router for uas11 to uas19 and a companion for uas11 to
# uas14. A longer list than four flies the extra vehicles with a router and no
# ROS stack behind it, and ./px4sim says so when it reads this line.
#
# The quotes matter. Both ./px4sim and docker compose read this file, and the
# shell needs them to keep the four names in one value.
#
# A simulated vehicle is its real counterpart plus ten, so this fleet is uas11
# to uas14 and it can fly beside the real uas1 to uas4. Vehicle N takes MAVLink
# system id N, ROS namespace /uas${N}, ROS domain 60 + N, MAVLink port
# 14550 + N offboard and 14402 onboard, and streams named after the number.
# docs/uas-contract.md is the whole map.
#
# Every stream is one more encode on the GPU. A fleet of four is 20 streams.
# Shorten this list first when the machine cannot keep up.
UAS_FLEET="chimera_v3"
# Which cameras each vehicle serves, one entry for each. A GPU allows a
# handful of encoding sessions at once, and every camera costs one for its
# full stream and one for its scaled one, so a fleet of four cannot serve
# everything. Past the limit a stream fails to start and never appears.
#   gimbal   what the detector reads: rgb on a v3, pilot on a v2
#   all      every camera the model declares
#   a list   rgb, pilot or thermal, comma separated
# One entry for each vehicle, or one for all of them. Turn a single vehicle
# up without touching the rest:
#   UAS_STREAMS="all gimbal gimbal gimbal"
UAS_STREAMS="gimbal"

# Set UAS11_MODEL to v2 or v3 to override the airframe of one companion. It has
# to agree with UAS_FLEET: the simulator would serve pilot11 while ds_node
# opened rgb11, and the detector would simply never receive a frame.

# Camera fields of view, degrees, one for each vehicle in the same order. These
# belong to the vehicle rather than to the mark: uas13 and uas14 are both v2 and
# carry different lenses.
#
# The authority is the calibration file that `cam_info.calibration_file` names
# in each vehicle's 5g_drone parameter file. These are those files reduced to
# one number, 2*atan(width / (2*fx)), and this is the only copy in this
# repository. Re-derive them when a lens changes.
#
#   uas11  v3  SCF4 zoom, widest           56.06
#   uas12  v3  assumed the same as uas11   56.06
#   uas13  v2  90deg-cil034                85.25
#   uas14  v2  28deg-cil142                25.98
# The field of view the gimbal camera RENDERS, per vehicle. On a v3 this is
# the widest the lens reaches, because a narrower zoom preset is the middle
# of it: gz-sim cannot change a camera's field of view once the world is
# loaded. On a v2 the lens is fixed and this is simply what it sees.
UAS_GIMBAL_HFOV_DEG="56.06 56.06 85.25 25.98"
# The zoom presets a v3 lens reaches. The lens is a 1x, 3x and 10x framing, and
# these are those magnifications as fields of view: focal length scales with
# magnification, so the angle is 2*atan(width / (2 * mag * fx_wide)). Wide is
# the aircraft's measured wide calibration, and the other two follow from it.
# The aircraft's own narrow and mid calibration files are placeholders and
# disagree; they are the lens's to fix, not this table's.
UAS_ZOOM_PRESETS="narrow=6.09 mid=20.13 wide=56.06"
# Where each framing puts the lens, in motor steps, zoom then focus. Taken from
# uas1_params.yaml so the simulated lens is driven through the same numbers the
# aircraft is. The emulated SCF4 controller moves these counters and the
# companion recalls these positions.
UAS_ZOOM_STEPS="narrow=29000,32380 mid=34500,32980 wide=40000,31140"
# Travel of each axis in motor steps, low then high, and the step the homing
# datum sits at. The emulated controller puts its photo-interrupter at the
# datum and its stops just outside the travel, so homing lands where the
# companion's zoom.limits.* say it will. Also from uas1_params.yaml.
UAS_ZOOM_TRAVEL="zoom=29000,40000 focus=29500,33500"
UAS_ZOOM_DATUM="zoom=32000 focus=32000"
# The emulated controller listens on this port plus the vehicle number, inside
# the sim container. The companion opens socket://sim:<port> in place of the
# USB serial device the aircraft has. uas11 is 5911.
UAS_ZOOM_PORT_BASE=5900
# Which framing each vehicle's lens comes up at, after its startup homing. A
# dash means the vehicle has no zoom. Change it in flight from Foxglove, or
# with ./px4sim zoom 11 wide.
UAS_ZOOM="mid mid - -"
# Thermal, from 32deg-20640A032_6IARX: 31.03 on uas13, 29.75 on the rest.
UAS_THERMAL_HFOV_DEG="29.75 29.75 31.03 29.75"
# PLACEHOLDER. The v3 down-facing camera has no calibration file, so no
# measurement exists. 25.98 is the value uas4_params.yaml already uses as a
# placeholder for this camera, reused here so the two agree. Every footprint
# and ground projection this camera feeds rests on a guess until somebody
# calibrates it.
UAS_DOWN_HFOV_DEG="25.98 25.98 25.98 25.98"
# Metres between vehicles on the ground at spawn.
UAS_SPACING_M=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- the scenario
# SCENE picks a world file from modules/sim/scenes/worlds/<SCENE>.sdf
# SCENARIO picks a target file from modules/sim/scenes/scenarios/<SCENARIO>.yaml
# AIRFRAME is the PX4 SYS_AUTOSTART id. 4019 is the gimbal-enabled x500.
#
# These lines carry the coordinates with them. The world origin and the
# survey marker are read from the scenario file (home_* and fiducial_*), and
# from the world file (<spherical_coordinates>) when the scenario has none.
# No coordinate belongs here: a second copy can disagree with the scene, and
# then the mission flies somewhere else and looks correct while it does it.
# `./px4sim origin` prints what this pair resolves to.
# On a real machine this pair is the site the aircraft stands on, and both
# machines carry the same one: SCENE=uroc and SCENARIO=uroc_casualties at the
# UMD test site. Both empty is a bench outside any surveyed site, which draws
# no terrain and publishes no ground truth. `./px4sim genscene` builds a scene
# for a site that has none, and chimera-deploy's `setup_git_server.sh scenes`
# sends the built scenes to every aircraft.
SCENE=lorton
AIRFRAME=4019
SCENARIO=lorton_casualties

# Gazebo GUI. Set to 0 for a headless run.
GZ_GUI=0
# Real-time factor. 1 is real time. 2 runs the physics twice as fast.
SIM_SPEED_FACTOR=1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------- video
# The host side of the RTSP port. A ground-station machine can already run a
# restreamer for the real fleet on 8554, and the start then stops at
# video-router with every service after it unstarted. Move only the host side:
# inside simnet every consumer dials video-router:8554 regardless, so QGC and
# the companions never notice. `./px4sim view` and the printed URLs follow
# this value.
# RTSP_HOST_PORT=8654

# The video encoder. Empty probes the encoders and takes the first that works,
# H.265 before H.264, which is what the aircraft sends. Name your own to skip
# the probe, and give the parser its output needs. Quote it: the value holds
# spaces, and ./px4sim reads this file with the shell.
#   VIDEO_ENCODER="x264enc tune=zerolatency speed-preset=ultrafast bitrate=4000"
#   VIDEO_PARSER=h264parse
VIDEO_ENCODER=
VIDEO_PARSER=h264parse

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- who gets MAVLink
# Each router sends its offboard endpoint to GCS_ADDRESS on port 14550 + N,
# which is 14561 upwards for a simulated vehicle and is what a ground
# mavlink-router from chimera-deploy/local expects.
#
# Both lines below are commented out on purpose. compose.yaml defaults them to
# the ground station and the QGC container on the simnet, and its defaults
# follow SIMNET_PREFIX. A literal address here would not, so setting
# SIMNET_PREFIX would send every vehicle's telemetry to a host that is not on
# the network, with no error on either side.
#
# Set one only to reach a ground station or a QGroundControl outside this stack.
# GCS_ADDRESS=10.200.142.210
# QGC_ADDRESS=10.200.142.224

# The simnet subnet. The addresses deconflict with the fleet. The subnet does
# not. A bridge on 10.200.142.0/24 shadows the whole real range on a host that
# is itself on the radio network, .60 to .64 included. Set this on such a host.
# t500 is on that network, so the line is not optional there. Set it before
# the first start.
# SIMNET_PREFIX=172.28.0

# A ground station heartbeat, so the PX4 data link loss failsafe stays quiet
# with no ground station attached. 0 to test that failsafe.
KEEPALIVE=1
